  "job": "Rings wide notes over the enemy front line; anyone struck by two of them stops cold.",
  "difficulty": 1,
  "lore": "Vashil keeps seven small bells on a chalk ring above his visor and strikes them with a rod as long as his arm. Every one of them is tuned a little wrong on purpose. A bell struck once makes people turn. A bell struck twice makes them stop. He learned this in the Glass Belfry, ringing the morning change for a valley that never found its morning, and the only third stroke he rings is the one that ends the fight. He is polite, quick and a little early to everything. His bells are early too.",
